title: Graph Coloring
text: E = {ab, ad, bc, cd, ce, de, df, ef, eg, fg, fh, gh}, k = 3, b = G, g = R. The cartographers get four.
trick: vertices a-h in a row, each turned one primary by a multi-filter's rotation; each edge is a fixed AND gate where two vertices' diagonals cross, so equal colours fire it into its black target. White fires too, and the multi-filter cannot go dark. The triangle strip cde, def, efg, fgh forces c = f, d = g and e = h, nothing follows locally from the two fixed vertices, then g = R gives d = R, so c = B through b = G, and a closes the 4-cycle abcd as B
motif: a row of eight sockets with gates above and below where diagonals cross
expect: recolours>=6
